  "headline": "Home of the Golden Temple",
  "short_description": "Amritsar is centred on the Golden Temple, Sikhism's holiest shrine, and the historic Jallianwala Bagh and Wagah Border.",
  "about": "Founded by the fourth Sikh Guru, Guru Ram Das, in 1577, Amritsar is the spiritual centre of Sikhism and a city steeped in modern Indian history.\n\nLocated in Punjab near the India-Pakistan border, in the fertile plains of the Beas-Ravi doab.\n\nRenowned for Punjabi hospitality, Bhangra music and dance, and some of North India's most famous food.\n\nThe spiritual centre of Sikhism, home to the Golden Temple (Harmandir Sahib).",
  "history": "Grew around the excavation of the sacred pool (Amrit Sarovar) and the building of the Golden Temple; site of the 1919 Jallianwala Bagh massacre, a landmark event in India's independence movement.",
  "history_verified": false,
  "transportation": "- Sri Guru Ram Dass Jee International Airport (airport)\n- Amritsar Junction (railway)\n- Amritsar Bus Stand (bus terminal)",
  "travel_info": "Languages: Punjabi, Hindi, English\nBudget: mid range",
  "best_time_text": "October to March",
